    {
      "id": 3,
      "kind": "F_retrieval",
      "payload": "{\"characters\":0,\"documents\":[],\"llm_tokens\":0,\"query\":\"A locality SIMD OpenMP\"}",
      "created": 1792152828.5123
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research coarse-grained CPU parallelism. Partition target bodies i into contiguous ranges across at most four workers, preserving each body's ascending j accumulation. Use threading supported by the unchanged build; compare one, two and four workers. Prefer a persistent team across all ten iterations. Require a barrier between force calculation and position integration, and another before the next force pass. Positions must remain immutable throughout each force pass; velocity writes are disjoint. Initially retain the existing layout and arithmetic to isolate threading gains. Measure end-to-end performance, including worker startup, and retain a general small-workload serial fallback only if measurements justify it.\",\"B\":\"Research order-preserving ARM64 SIMD and instruction-level parallelism, initially single-threaded. Process a small block of independent target bodies together, broadcasting each source body's coordinates while advancing j in its original order. Vectorize across targets, not through a reassociated source reduction. Compare scalar unrolling with supported ARM64 SIMD and handle all tails correctly. Preserve the float squared-distance calculation, binary64 sqrt and reciprocal, conversion to float, and subsequent multiplication/accumulation semantics, including existing contraction behavior. Do not substitute sqrtf, approximate reciprocal-square-root, or fast reductions. Measure register pressure and any packing costs; preserve the external body layout.\",\"C\":\"Research exact symmetric-pair reuse as an alternative force kernel. Evaluate one distance and reciprocal per unordered pair, maintaining separate force accumulators. Explore an increasing-i triangular sweep with increasing j>i: contributions from lower-index sources must already have arrived in ascending order, followed by the diagonal contribution and then higher-index sources. This can preserve each body's original summation order while nearly halving expensive distance evaluations. Compute reverse-direction coordinate differences explicitly rather than merely negating an already-rounded force. Prove arithmetic equivalence under the fixed build, and retain the original kernel for exceptional states where reuse is not proven safe, including nonfinite coordinates; reconsider this guard every timestep. Keep positions immutable and preserve diagonal contributions. Start serial and measure reciprocal savings against scratch-array traffic. Reject the approach if exactness cannot be established.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only correctness-validated artifacts within the existing evaluation budget. Compare the strongest standalone candidates first, then prioritize combining A's target partitioning with B's independent-target kernel, ensuring disjoint blocks and correct tails. Treat C as an alternative algorithm: naively parallelizing its triangular sweep introduces races and changes accumulation order. Attempt combinations with C only with an explicit dependency-preserving design. Remeasure every integration end to end; gains are not additive, and the best standalone program may remain best. Preserve input's integer count followed by six-float records, output records without a count, ten timesteps, DT and SOFTENING. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, target and budgets unchanged. Deliver the fastest measured correct candidate with its actual validation and timing evidence.\",\"analysis\":\"Only Problem C and src/nbody.c are relevant. The baseline passed four cases and averaged 0.662682 seconds across three tightly clustered samples. No profile, numerical tolerance, or optimized measurements are supplied. The likely bottleneck is ten quadratic all-pairs force passes, particularly square root/division and serial accumulation. The target provides four ARM64 CPU cores and no GPU. Importantly, sqrt and the reciprocal currently execute in double precision before inv_dist is rounded to float. Prioritize CPU parallelism, ordered SIMD, and carefully proven pair reuse; do not infer permission for numerical approximations from four passing cases. Every valid input must remain correct.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"a54ea787a94cdeed40ab65616198eff29efa75955692848f392dbca2d9e8c937\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research coarse-grained CPU parallelism. Partition target bodies i into contiguous ranges across at most four workers, preserving each body's ascending j accumulation. Use threading supported by the unchanged build; compare one, two and four workers. Prefer a persistent team across all ten iterations. Require a barrier between force calculation and position integration, and another before the next force pass. Positions must remain immutable throughout each force pass; velocity writes are disjoint. Initially retain the existing layout and arithmetic to isolate threading gains. Measure end-to-end performance, including worker startup, and retain a general small-workload serial fallback only if measurements justify it.\",\"B\":\"Research order-preserving ARM64 SIMD and instruction-level parallelism, initially single-threaded. Process a small block of independent target bodies together, broadcasting each source body's coordinates while advancing j in its original order. Vectorize across targets, not through a reassociated source reduction. Compare scalar unrolling with supported ARM64 SIMD and handle all tails correctly. Preserve the float squared-distance calculation, binary64 sqrt and reciprocal, conversion to float, and subsequent multiplication/accumulation semantics, including existing contraction behavior. Do not substitute sqrtf, approximate reciprocal-square-root, or fast reductions. Measure register pressure and any packing costs; preserve the external body layout.\",\"C\":\"Research exact symmetric-pair reuse as an alternative force kernel. Evaluate one distance and reciprocal per unordered pair, maintaining separate force accumulators. Explore an increasing-i triangular sweep with increasing j>i: contributions from lower-index sources must already have arrived in ascending order, followed by the diagonal contribution and then higher-index sources. This can preserve each body's original summation order while nearly halving expensive distance evaluations. Compute reverse-direction coordinate differences explicitly rather than merely negating an already-rounded force. Prove arithmetic equivalence under the fixed build, and retain the original kernel for exceptional states where reuse is not proven safe, including nonfinite coordinates; reconsider this guard every timestep. Keep positions immutable and preserve diagonal contributions. Start serial and measure reciprocal savings against scratch-array traffic. Reject the approach if exactness cannot be established.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only correctness-validated artifacts within the existing evaluation budget. Compare the strongest standalone candidates first, then prioritize combining A's target partitioning with B's independent-target kernel, ensuring disjoint blocks and correct tails. Treat C as an alternative algorithm: naively parallelizing its triangular sweep introduces races and changes accumulation order. Attempt combinations with C only with an explicit dependency-preserving design. Remeasure every integration end to end; gains are not additive, and the best standalone program may remain best. Preserve input's integer count followed by six-float records, output records without a count, ten timesteps, DT and SOFTENING. Keep tests, oracle, compiler, target and budgets unchanged. Deliver the fastest measured correct candidate with its actual validation and timing evidence.\",\"analysis\":\"Only Problem C and src/nbody.c are relevant. The baseline passed four cases and averaged 0.662682 seconds across three tightly clustered samples. No profile, numerical tolerance, or optimized measurements are supplied. The likely bottleneck is ten quadratic all-pairs force passes, particularly square root/division and serial accumulation. The target provides four ARM64 CPU cores and no GPU. Importantly, sqrt and the reciprocal currently execute in double precision before inv_dist is rounded to float. Prioritize CPU parallelism, ordered SIMD, and carefully proven pair reuse; do not infer permission for numerical approximations from four passing cases. Every valid input must remain correct.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"nonce\":\"024a3aae325f40418814005488392d54\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"a54ea787a94cdeed40ab65616198eff29efa75955692848f392dbca2d9e8c937\",\"session_id\":\"c0e9dfffccc040969abe9f6f54635671\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"ba0652dca51a0275fa0f9df32dec2d0e5d5469f050e3c36329050fad54a23c9e\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":4096,\"input_tokens\":10387,\"output_tokens\":8506,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":7768}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":18893,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
